(7663807, 1248944, 251422, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by primabarbara:</b></div><hr/><i> This is so fabulous, Susan! Focus, light, frozen action, the pop of red - just great<br/>Congrats on the frontpage finish!<br/>I know how much effort it takes to create a shot like this - that\''s why I never tried it...<br/> <br/>And considering the low votes:<br/>You better get used to it. There are several voters who use the complete range of voting possibilities from 1-10. But I try to tell me that this isn\''t bad as long as they do it on <u>all</u> entries - it has an effect on the average score but not that much on the ranking (at least that is my way to cope with low votes) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>As I said, I''m pretty new to the site. Just joined last year.  The low scores don''t bother me as much as bewilder me.  I shoot because I like the creativity and the themes  enable me to be creative and have a variety in my photography.  What I don''t understand is what a low score is based on.  As far as I can tell there isn''t any judging criteria on the site.  What is the criteria for giving a 1?  In my opinion, no photo deserves a 1 - if there is no criteria to give that score.  I wonder if anyone has ever considered creating judging criteria so that scores are based on something concrete.  Just a thought.  Not so much for my photo but when I see blue ribbon winners that were scored with a 1, I wonder what the low score was based on.</td>', 'Originally posted by primabarbara: This is so fabulous, Susan! Focus, light, frozen action, the pop of red - just greatCongrats on the frontpage finish!I know how much effort it takes to create a shot like this - that\''s why I never tried it... And considering the low votes:You better get used to it. There are several voters who use the complete range of voting possibilities from 1-10. But I try to tell me that this isn\''t bad as long as they do it on all entries - it has an effect on the average score but not that much on the ranking (at least that is my way to cope with low votes)   As I said, I''m pretty new to the site. Just joined last year.  The low scores don''t bother me as much as bewilder me.  I shoot because I like the creativity and the themes  enable me to be creative and have a variety in my photography.  What I don''t understand is what a low score is based on.  As far as I can tell there isn''t any judging criteria on the site.  What is the criteria for giving a 1?  In my opinion, no photo deserves a 1 - if there is no criteria to give that score.  I wonder if anyone has ever considered creating judging criteria so that scores are based on something concrete.  Just a thought.  Not so much for my photo but when I see blue ribbon winners that were scored with a 1, I wonder what the low score was based on.', '2020-05-25 07:27:01.000000', NULL, 0),
