do it on all entries - it has an effect on the average score but not that much on the ranking (at least that is my way to cope with low votes)   As I said, I''m pretty new to the site. Just joined last year.  The low scores don''t bother me as much as bewilder me.  I shoot because I like the creativity and the themes  enable me to be creative and have a variety in my photography.  What I don''t understand is what a low score is based on.  As far as I can tell there isn''t any judging criteria on the site.  What is the criteria for giving a 1?  In my opinion, no photo deserves a 1 - if there is no criteria to give that score.  I wonder if anyone has ever considered creating judging criteria so that scores are based on something concrete.  Just a thought.  Not so much for my photo but when I see blue ribbon winners that were scored with a 1, I wonder what the low score was based on.', '2020-05-25 07:27:30.000000', NULL, 0),
