(7663823, 1249681, 173844, '<td valign="top">Interesting, fun, utterly natural.  The red''s part of life, the greens and blues are lovely.</td>', 'Interesting, fun, utterly natural.  The red''s part of life, the greens and blues are lovely.', '2020-05-25 10:58:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(7663824, 1249484, 173844, '<td valign="top">Stunning.  Fades out of focus like a dream.  A delicate assassin.  Imagine what it''s like to be the caterpillar victim.  Can we shrug our shoulders and muse, he or she hasn''t consciousness as we determine it, is therefor insensible to pain?  Maybe no dreams, and so no nightmares?  These lines of inquiry can be overwhelming, so we save our sanity be backing off.  At least I do.  In the end, self-preservation.<br/>One of my favorites of your wonderful plumbing of the world of insects.  And my personal favorite of this challenge.</td>', 'Stunning.  Fades out of focus like a dream.  A delicate assassin.  Imagine what it''s like to be the caterpillar victim.  Can we shrug our shoulders and muse, he or she hasn''t consciousness as we determine it, is therefor insensible to pain?  Maybe no dreams, and so no nightmares?  These lines of inquiry can be overwhelming, so we save our sanity be backing off.  At least I do.  In the end, self-preservation.One of my favorites of your wonderful plumbing of the world of insects.  And my personal favorite of this challenge.', '2020-05-25 11:16:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(7663906, 1248944, 67145, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Beaubeau:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by primabarbara:</b></div><hr/><i> This is so fabulous, Susan! Focus, light, frozen action, the pop of red - just great<br/>Congrats on the frontpage finish!<br/>I know how much effort it takes to create a shot like this - that\''s why I never tried it...<br/> <br/>And considering the low votes:<br/>You better get used to it. There are several voters who use the complete range of voting possibilities from 1-10. But I try to tell me that this isn\''t bad as long as they do it on <u>all</u> entries - it has an effect on the average score but not that much on the ranking (at least that is my way to cope with low votes) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>As I said, I''m pretty new to the site. Just joined last year.  The low scores don''t bother me as much as bewilder me.  I shoot because I like the creativity and the themes  enable me to be creative and have a variety in my photography.  What I don''t understand is what a low score is based on.  As far as I can tell there isn''t any judging criteria on the site.  What is the criteria for giving a 1?  In my opinion, no photo deserves a 1 - if there is no criteria to give that score.  I wonder if anyone has ever considered creating judging criteria so that scores are based on something concrete.  Just a thought.  Not so much for my photo but when I see blue ribbon winners that were scored with a 1, I wonder what the low score was based on. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>i''ve heard on the grapevine that sometimes a 1 is given by mistake by someone voting on their phone or something .. so that they go to give a 1 and a 0 but only the 1 gets recorded .. i feel that they should remove that possibility and start the voting off at 2 .. :)</td>', 'Originally posted by Beaubeau: Originally posted by primabarbara: This is so fabulous, Susan! Focus, light, frozen action, the pop of red - just greatCongrats on the frontpage finish!I know how much effort it takes to create a shot like this - that\''s why I never tried it... And considering the low votes:You better get used to it. There are several voters who use the complete range of voting possibilities from 1-10. But I try to tell me that this isn\''t bad as long as they do it on all entries - it has an effect on the average score but not that much on the ranking (at least that is my way to cope with low votes)   As I said, I''m pretty new to the site. Just joined last year.  The low scores don''t bother me as much as bewilder me.  I shoot because I like the creativity and the themes  enable me to be creative and have a variety in my photography.  What I don''t understand is what a low score is based on.  As far as I can tell there isn''t any judging criteria on the site.  What is the criteria for giving a 1?  In my opinion, no photo deserves a 1 - if there is no criteria to give that score.  I wonder if anyone has ever considered creating judging criteria so that scores are based on something concrete.  Just a thought.  Not so much for my photo but when I see blue ribbon winners that were scored with a 1, I wonder what the low score was based on.   i''ve heard on the grapevine that sometimes a 1 is given by mistake by someone voting on their phone or something .. so that they go to give a 1 and a 0 but only the 1 gets recorded .. i feel that they should remove that possibility and start the voting off at 2 .. :)', '2020-05-25 18:02:18.000000', NULL, 0),
